<title>USA: Property Capital to sell Chicago City Centre.</title>
<headline>Property Capital to sell Chicago City Centre.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property Capital Trust said Tuesday it has agreed to sell City Centre Holiday Inn in Chicago for about $20 million, resulting in a gain of about $18 million, or $1.92 per share.</p>
<p>The sale is scheduled to close in January 1997. It is to be sold to the lessee, who was not identified.</p>
<p>Property Capital said it anticipates distributing the proceeds to shareholders. In the 1996 fiscal year, income from the property was $1.83 million.</p>
</text>
